const defaultText={"heroLead":"Creative PR student building her way into motorsport.","heroMeta":"I AM LOOKING FOR A 3-MONTH INTERNSHIP · MOTORSPORT · EVENTS · SPORTS MARKETING · AGENCY","about1":"I’m Léa, a third-year Public Relations student based in Belgium, with a strong interest in communication, events, content and brands. I love being versatile and doing a lot of things, learning from life, travels and other people.","about2":"I’ve always been drawn to projects that bring people together ; from large-scale festivals and premium events to social media content and creative concepts.","about3":"Through my studies and professional experiences, I’ve learned to work across different sides of communication and the event sector : planning, creating, coordinating, communicating and, most importantly, adapting.","about4":"Today, I’m looking for a 3 months internship where I can learn from a new environment mixing sports, communication, events, social medias,.. ","ardentes":"My second-year Public Relations internship took me behind the scenes of Les Ardentes Festival, where communication meets live entertainment, community and large-scale event production. During this Internship, I saw the before and the during of a big event like this. I had the opportunity to work on the website, the social media & also the mailing. My work was versatile and I loved that !","chant":"Alongside my studies, I’ve been working at Chant d’Éole, a Belgian champagne estate, in a premium hospitality and event environment. I work as mush during the events as at the gourmet restaurant. My skills in this job are versatile and this job asks me to be very professional and listening !","motoIntro":"I’m interested in motorsport because it brings together many of the things I enjoy most about communication  and life : brands, people, live experiences, content, cars, storytelling and high-pressure environments.","conception":"Communication & operations lead · Sold out · 200+ guests · 30 models · 9 creators","conceptionDescription":"La Conception was a fashion show I conceptualized and organized with 4 other people. The idea was to bring together fashion, music and creative people in a single event. As Communication & Operations Lead, I coordinated the team, managed event logistics and led promotional efforts to deliver a sold-out event welcoming over 250 guests, featuring 30+ models and 9 creators.","conceptionCategory":"EVENT / COMMUNICATION","women":"Women2Women is an international initiative designed to bring young women together, encourage cross-cultural dialogue and empower the next generation of female leaders. Through shared experiences, discussions and collaborative activities, the program creates opportunities to explore leadership, develop new perspectives and build meaningful connections beyond cultural and geographical boundaries.\n\nAt its core, Women2Women is about creating a space where young women can exchange ideas, learn from one another and reflect on their role in shaping the future. By bringing together different experiences, backgrounds and ambitions, the initiative encourages participants to challenge themselves, strengthen their confidence and discover new ways to contribute to their communities.\n\nI had the opportunity to be selected in 2022 for the online program during the covid's period and in 2025 for the program in Boston where I got to be alumni. That was one of the best experience of my life, it helps being more confident, having more idea of what it is to be an empowered women in a patriarchal world. During this program I had the opportunity to meet a lot of people, to make contact in professional fields and finally to build and present an action plan which was my first podcast : \"sisterhood stories\". ","womenIntro":"Women2Women is an international initiative designed to bring young women together, encourage cross-cultural dialogue and empower the next generation of female leaders. Through shared experiences, discussions and collaborative activities, the program creates opportunities to explore leadership, develop new perspectives and build meaningful connections beyond cultural and geographical boundaries.","womenDevelopment":"\nAt its core, Women2Women is about creating a space where young women can exchange ideas, learn from one another and reflect on their role in shaping the future. By bringing together different experiences, backgrounds and ambitions, the initiative encourages participants to challenge themselves, strengthen their confidence and discover new ways to contribute to their communities.","womenTakeaway":"I had the opportunity to be selected in 2022 for the online program during the covid's period and in 2025 for the program in Boston where I got to be alumni. That was one of the best experience of my life, it helps being more confident, having more idea of what it is to be an empowered women in a patriarchal world. During this program I had the opportunity to meet a lot of people, to make contact in professional fields and finally to build and present an action plan which was my first podcast : \"sisterhood stories\". ","journalismTitle1":"INTERVIEW BENITOWSHOW","journalismText1":"A studio interview for the cinema students' of my school where I presented a showcase of a belgian music group, I prepared myself all of my speech, my questions etc with the public informations about the artists","journalismTitle2":"INTERVIEW AVERAGE ROB","journalismText2":"An interview of Average Rob in English during a philanthropy event in Brussels organised by king Baudouin Fondation where I was accredited to create content and interviewing some speakers !","podcastTitle":"PODCAST","podcastText":"2 different projects but the same willing to share toughs, ideas and conversation which can be deep or just good vibes","sportTitle":"SPORT CONTENT","sportText":"From sharing my own sports journey through vlogs and social content to capturing game-day moments and creating Instagram Stories for my school’s basketball team.","schoolTitle":"SCHOOL CONTENT","schoolText":"Creating content for my school’s Student Council, with a focus on making information more engaging, accessible and relevant to students. I did also some school vlogs on my instagram that my school uses to promote the PR cursus !","spaTag":"SPA-FRANCORCHAMPS · 2025","spaTitle":"FORMULA 1\nRACE WEEKEND","spaText":"My first Belgian Grand Prix in 2025 introduced me to the support races beyond Formula 1 and made me fall in love with the Spa-Francorchamps circuit. I captured the experience through photography and a YouTube vlog.","twentyFourTag":"SPA-FRANCORCHAMPS · 2026","twentyFourTitle":"24 HOURS\nOF SPA","twentyFourText":"I spent three days at the 2026 24 Hours of Spa with my best friend, capturing the atmosphere through photography and content creation. Being able to get close to the cars and explore the garages made the experience even more special.","podcast1Title":"Brut.e","podcast2Title":"Sisterhood stories","podcast1":"Brut.e is a personal and introspective podcast exploring emotions, personal growth and the realities of being human but also some tough that came in my head. Through honest conversations with friends and solo reflections, it creates space for vulnerability, self-discovery and perspectives that often go unheard.","podcast2":"Born from my experience in the Women2Women program, Sisterhood Stories was created to offer women a safe space to share their stories, experiences and struggles. In a chaotic world where navigating life as a woman can still be challenging, the project aimed to foster sisterhood, mutual support and a sense of belonging.","creativeTitle":"CREATIVE CONTENT","creativeText":"Personal photo, video and short-form experiments developed to explore visual storytelling."};

